  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Activity under preparation Study on Rectification and Upgradation of the  Common Effluent Treatment Plant at the Savar Tannery Industrial Estate</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;The expected outputs of this contract are as follows:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&#xBF; A study to:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;(a) Identify the areas of rectification and upgradation of the existing Common Effluent Treatment Plant (CETP) in line with LWG standards or comparable international standards including design, drawing and technical specifications (detailed survey assessment).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;(b) Assess the need and requirements for an expansion of the existing CETP or construction of a second CETP based on project growth (and assumptions) for the Savar Tannery Industrial Estate (capacity assessment for the current CETP and a needs assessment for a second CETP)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;(c) Assess the conveyor system to channel the flow of wastewater from the tanneries to the CETP, including design, drawing and technical specifications, as well as recommendations on how to calculate and sub-divide the cost of operations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;(d) Analyse the potential for waste management related value chain development, i.e. waste to wealth (value chain analysis for solid waste treatment).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&#xBF; A dissemination event for sharing the findings&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
